    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204723": {
      "title": "Academic Counselor",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Academic Counselor McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Academic Counselor Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Academic Counselor Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Access & Support Serv Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $40,160.00 - $40,160.00 Position ID: 204723 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. This position has a budgeted hiring rate of $40,160. The position is classified as an A2. The A2 salary band for all full-time, 9-month positions at the college with this classification have a minimum rate of $32,910 and a maximum rate of $47,390.40. The actual schedule for exempt positions may vary based on the workload and responsibilities assigned. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: The Academic Counselor provides individualized academic support and case management for students with disabilities, ensuring equitable access to educational opportunities and compliance with Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Managing a caseload of 13 to 17 students, the counselor develops and implements personalized success plans, monitors academic progress, addresses academic and personal barriers, and coordinates support services. Through ongoing guidance, skill development, and advocacy-focused coaching, the counselor empowers students to strengthen academic performance, build independence and self-advocacy skills, and persist toward degree completion. Key Responsibilities The Academic Counselor supports students by helping them identify learning preferences, develop effective study strategies, and implement academic adjustments to meet the demands of college coursework. Through weekly meetings with those in the Elevate Program, Academic Counselors work with a case load of students monitoring academic progress, facilitates goal setting and skill development, and provides accountability and intervention strategies to promote student success, retention, and persistence. The role collaborates closely with faculty, academic leaders, and student support professionals to enhance student learning and engagement, while serving as an advocate and liaison to ensure access to appropriate accommodations and resources. Additionally, the counselor fosters self-advocacy, independence, and self-determination, coordinates referrals to campus and community support services, maintains confidential student records and documentation, communicates with authorized family members in compliance with FERPA, and performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Master's Degree in Counseling, Special Education, or related field preferred. Bachelor's degree required. Extensive knowledge of the Federal Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 as they relate to postsecondary education. Experience mentoring students with disabilities, preferably in higher education. Knowledge of psychoeducational tests/instruments and the ability to interpret psychoeducational reports. Excellent organizational skills as well as oral and written communication skills. Ability to work effectively to meet deadlines. Ability to use computers for word processing data, data entry, and related tasks. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: To apply For a complete job description including essential responsibilities and to apply, please visit the college's employment webpage. Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
    },
    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204701": {
      "title": "Director of Pick STEM Center",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Director of Pick STEM Center McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Director of Pick STEM Center Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Pick STEM Center Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: STEM Center Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $74,000.00 - $74,000.00 Position ID: 204701 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. This position has a budgeted hiring rate of $74,000. The position is classified as an A4. The A4 salary band for all full-time, 12-month positions at the college with this classification have a minimum rate of $50,000 and a maximum rate of $93,780. The actual schedule for exempt positions may vary based on the workload and responsibilities assigned. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Reporting to the Senior Associate Vice President of Student Success, the Director of the STEM Learning Center provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for services designed to promote student achievement, persistence, and success in STEM disciplines. The Director is responsible for the management and continuous improvement of tutoring, supplemental instruction, academic support programming, student staff development, and collaborative initiatives that enhance learning outcomes for STEM students. Working closely with faculty, academic departments, and student success partners, the Director develops and implements evidence-based strategies that foster academic excellence, equitable access to support services, and student engagement. Key Responsibilities Leadership and Program Management Provides strategic leadership and operational oversight of the STEM Learning Center, developing goals, policies, programs, and assessment initiatives that support student success and align with institutional priorities. Collaborates with faculty, academic leaders, and student support services to enhance learning opportunities, promote equitable access, and meet the diverse needs of STEM students. Oversees outreach, marketing, and online engagement efforts to increase awareness and utilization of services, while managing facilities, technology, budgets, supplies, and learning resources. Monitors program effectiveness, analyzes student outcomes and usage data, and prepares reports and recommendations to support continuous improvement, institutional reporting, and accreditation efforts. Provide professional development opportunities about best practices in STEM pedagogy and inclusive teaching in STEM. Provides expertise and leadership in STEM education by supporting faculty through professional development, consultation, and guidance on effective STEM pedagogy, learning support strategies, and inclusive teaching practices. Serves as a resource on emerging trends and best practices in STEM teaching and learning, contributes to institutional initiatives focused on student retention, persistence, and success, and may teach courses related to peer tutoring and academic support as needed. Coordinate tutoring efforts in STEM Oversees recruitment, hiring, training, scheduling, supervision, and evaluation of tutors. Manages tutoring programs, supplemental instruction, academic workshops, study groups, and related student support initiatives to promote academic success. Ensures accurate and compliant processing of employee timesheets and payroll records, and collaborates closely with faculty to support tutors facilitating co-remediation workshops. Other responsibilities as necessary Supports the STEM Learning Center's mission through collaboration on student success initiatives, STEM outreach and engagement programs, and campus-wide support services. Assists with admitted student events, STEM programming, and academic tutoring initiatives, while partnering with Student Success, Student Accessibility and Support Services (SASS), the Office of Student Belonging, and other campus stakeholders to enhance student support and develop new programs. May also advise student organizations and activities aligned with the center's educational and student development goals. Requirements: Master's Degree in Education, a STEM field, Higher Education Administrative, or Educational Leadership required. At least 3 years of experience in STEM, Academic Support Services, Learning Centers, or Tutoring programs required, expertise in STEM-related pedagogy preferred. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Excellent administrative, project organization and management skills. Strong interpersonal skills to interact with a diverse population of students, faculty, and staff. Experience working with students from underrepresented populations. Ability to set priorities and work independently. A demonstrable commitment to and expertise in promoting and sustaining a diverse and inclusive campus. Knowledge of learning management systems, tutoring management software, and student success technologies (i.e. - EAB Navigate360) preferred. Experience training and supporting peer tutors, certifying learning centers, or providing Supplemental Instruction preferred. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: To apply For a complete job description including essential responsibilities and to apply, please visit the college's employment webpage. Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
    },
    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204558": {
      "title": "AVI Cook-Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: AVI Cook-Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: AVI Cook-Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details AVI Cook-Food Service Student Worker, Federal Work Study Only Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Center for Experience and Oppo Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 8, 2026 Closes: Oct 13, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 204558 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Job Title: AVI Cook-Food Service Student Worker Effective Date: 07/08/2026 Reports to: AVI Managers Department: AVI Food Services Rate of Pay: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-Exempt Location of Position: Roj Student Center, McDaniel College, 2 College Hill, Westminster, MD 21157 Duration of Appointment: August 5, 2026 to May 25, 2027 Schedule: Schedule is at discretion of supervisor Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuous basis. Scope: Support food service functions for AVI on McDaniel College property. Responsibilities: Please customers by providing a pleasant dining experience Assemble, combine, and cook ingredients Maintain a sanitary kitchen Attend to the detail and presentation of each order Place and expedite orders Prepare ingredients by following recipes; slicing, cutting, chopping, mincing, stirring, whipping, and mixing ingredients Complete hot meal preparation by grilling, sautéing, roasting, frying, and broiling ingredients and assembling and refrigerating cold ingredients Adhere to proper food handling, sanitation, and safety procedures Maintain appropriate dating, labeling, and rotation of all food items Stores leftovers according to established standards Contribute to daily, holiday, and theme menus in collaboration with the team Requirements: Current undergraduate student at McDaniel College. Must have Federal Work Study as part of your Financial Aid package. Strong working knowledge of food preparation techniques, cooking methods, and safety and sanitation practices Familiarity with general kitchen equipment and appliances Strong work ethic and high energy level Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnanc