    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204856": {
      "title": "McDaniel Environmental Center Technician",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: McDaniel Environmental Center Technician - Campus Employment Only McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: McDaniel Environmental Center Technician - Campus Employment Only Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details McDaniel Environmental Center Technician - Campus Employment Only Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Environmental Studies Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Sep 23, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 204856 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Job Title: McDaniel Environmental Center Technician Effective Date: 09/16/2026 Reports to: Associate Professor of Environmental Studies Lecturer in Environmental Studies & Coordinator of MEC Department: Environmental Studies Rate of Pay: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-Exempt Location of Position: McDaniel Campus, McDaniel College, 2 College Hill, Westminster, MD 21157 Duration of Appointment: August 5, 2026 to May 25, 2027 Schedule: Schedule is at discretion of supervisor Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuous basis. Scope: Serve as a student worker at the McDaniel Environmental Center and campus garden sites, including weeding, watering, path maintenance, harvesting, delivering produce and other duties as assigned. Responsibilities: Participate in a short orientation with supervisor and ENV Food Fellows, learning both the physical space of the campus garden and reviewing safety guidelines for growing and harvesting produce for consumption by others. Participate in a weekly team coordination meeting with supervisor and the ENV Food Fellows to review weekly tasks and upcoming events. Maintain viability of garden space through regular weeding, watering, pest control, and harvesting of produce; planting fall / biennial crops; and garden path and shed upkeep. Collect produce harvest and donation data in an online spreadsheet. Deliver produce harvest to on-campus storage and distribution locations, as needed. Practice safe use of hand tools (trowel, broadfork, shovel, rake, clippers, etc). Execute assigned work in a conscientious, safe, and efficient manner. Work in cooperation with site supervisor and ENV Food Fellows to fulfill campus garden goals. Support tours and service events at/of the garden sites. Interact with other campus garden partners, including but not limited to Grounds, Physical Plant, the Home on the Hill program, other McDaniel faculty, student organizations, and ENV student fellows and researchers. Trail maintenance Invasive species removal and tracking Other duties as assigned. Schedule: 12 hours per week (weekend and/or weekends- to be determined by the supervisor) Requirements: Current undergraduate student at McDaniel College. 2.0 GPA required; 2.5 or higher preferred. Failure to maintain GPA will result in review and a probationary period. Ability to understand, organize, and carry out detailed instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and independently. Interested in food systems, gardening, and/or nutrition. Ability to work outdoors in noise, heat, cold, odors, dirt, precipitation, etc. Ability to lift; carry; and move objects weighing up to 50 lbs. without assistance as well as being able to kneel; squat; reach above the head, at the waist, and below the knees. Ability to repetitively grasp and manipulate objects of varying size and weight requiring fine motor skills and hand-eye coordination. Ability to exert oneself physically over sustained periods of time to complete job activities. Ability to stand a minimum of 3 hours during the workday. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
